# PyTorch models
*.pt

*.json
# Case-review markup is design intent, not a build artifact — it has to version
# alongside the CAD source it comments on. See tools/casereview/.
!tools/casereview/comments.json
*.jpg
*.png
# ...except the phone app's resources: ic_launcher and friends are build INPUTS
# for the APK (generated once by apps/dustyphone/tools/make_icons.py), not CAD
# renders.
!apps/**/*.png
yolov8n.onnx

# CAD build products. Regenerated from the *.step.py / caselib.py sources by
# cadgen, and published as release assets on a <part>/vN tag — see
# docs/REPO_PLAN.md §3. Ignored by EXTENSION, not by directory, because real
# sources (section_*.step.py, coupon_*.step.py, _sectionlib.py) live inside
# snaps/, print/ and review/ next to their exports.
*.step
*.stp
*.stl
*.3mf
*.glb
# ...except vendor/reference board models, which are INPUTS: a downloaded
# openmv-n6.step or ada-1578-lipo-500.step cannot be regenerated from anything
# in this repo. (REPO_PLAN §6 phase 5 moves these to /hd2 or `sarg cad get`.)
!**/ref/*.step
!**/ref/*.stp
!**/ref/*.STEP

# Device credentials — deployed to boards, never committed.
# (secrets_example.py / sdkconfig.defaults are the safe templates and DO get tracked.)
secrets.py
sdkconfig.secrets
# ESP-IDF: regenerated from sdkconfig.defaults + sdkconfig.secrets, embeds credentials
sdkconfig

# ESP-IDF regenerables (dependencies.lock pins them)
managed_components/
.idf_component_cache/
# archived databases / firmware binaries ride on disk, not in git
*.db
*.uf2
*.bin
*.npy
sdkconfig.old

# camera standard: generated bundles and per-board secrets
cameras/*/software/build/
cameras/*/software/app/secrets.py

# CAD generator caches and downloaded reference meshes (re-fetchable)
__cadgen__/
cameras/*/case/ref/*.glb
cameras/*/hardware/case/ref/*.glb

# CAD viewer caches (hidden GLB next to each STEP)
.*.step.glb
